"""Calculations written with derivatives, integrals and differential equations (``diff``, ``integrate``, ``odes``).

Derivatives and integrals are evaluated symbolically, so every quantity can still be solved for and the steps show the equation as
written and then its evaluated form. Differential equations (initial-value problems) are solved in closed form when SymPy can,
which keeps them fully rearrangeable, and numerically (with a plot of the solution) otherwise.
"""

from ..core import C, Calculation, V

